# Amendment #52 — primary-persona Agent-dispatch-as-scope
#                  wrapper (A8) + orchestrator
#                  activate_scope_with_spec IPC

2026-04-26. Closes the audit's "highest-leverage move" headline
(`docs/rebuild/plans/research/harness-usage-audit-2026-04-26.md`
§11): every persona-issued Agent dispatch now opens a
`ScopeSpec` over IPC and exercises the four-gate chain
(safety / reversibility / cost / orchestrator). Prior to this
amendment, exactly one production code path constructed a
`ScopeSpec` (`self-correction/src/spec_builder.py`); every
Agent dispatch ran outside `activate_scope` and outside the
wrap chain — cost-governance ledger empty, 80%-throttling
unreachable, `cost.status` IPC zero callers.

R1 ruling (locked by Luke 2026-04-26 — same pattern as the X
D5 ruling): the original plan §3 fence pinned to primary-
persona/ only was structurally incomplete. Empirical
verification (halt-surface report at
`.scratch/claude-output/A8-halt-surface-2026-04-26.md`) showed
`activate_scope` IPC takes only ids and the production
`spec_resolver` defaults to None for any scope not constructed
in-process by the orchestrator runtime — so the cost-gov
wrap's reservation step silently skips. Fence widened to
primary-persona/ + orchestrator/.

Surface added (primary-persona):

  - `primary-persona/src/dispatch_wrapper.py` (new) — D3.
    Exposes `dispatch_with_scope(...)` (single persona-callable
    surface per AC.A8.9) and helpers `_build_scope_spec` /
    `_infer_budget_from_duration` (D4 inline duration-rubric
    constant). Per-dispatch `IPCClient` open-and-close (D9).
    Fail-soft fallback when orchestrator unreachable
    (D1: NDJSON diagnostic to
    `<workspace>/.pos/dispatch-wrapper.log`, then proceed
    unwrapped — AC.A8.6). Default reversibility class
    compensatable (D2). Objective-id ambient-fallback to the
    amendment #39 tracker seed when caller omits (D5).
    Money-axis budget omitted by default (D6: time + tokens
    only; ledger accepts None money). Returns structured
    refusal as value, not exception (AC.A8.7).
  - `primary-persona/src/__init__.py` — re-exports
    `dispatch_with_scope`.

Surface added (orchestrator):

  - `orchestrator/src/orchestrator.py` —
    `activate_scope_with_spec(scope_id, objective_id,
    spec_payload)` Python surface (AC.A8.A1). Decodes spec
    via Pydantic, calls
    `scope_runtime.create(spec, scope_id=...)` in-process so
    the in-memory CostLedger subscriber sees the
    `ScopeCreated` event, then invokes the standard
    `activate_scope` path. IPC handler registered alongside
    the existing `activate_scope` (AC.A8.A2 unchanged).
    Includes a channel-registry hook so the workspace-bootstrap
    cost-governance adapter's `spec_resolver(scope_id)` finds
    the spec via the in-process create() path's projection.
  - Existing `activate_scope` IPC + Python surface unchanged
    per AC.A8.A2; `test_d5_bind_scope.py` stays green.

Behaviour:

  - The persona's `dispatch_with_scope(...)` opens a fresh
    `IPCClient`, builds a `ScopeSpec` from the dispatch shape,
    calls `activate_scope_with_spec` over IPC, awaits the
    gate-chain verdict. On approval, runs the underlying
    `Agent` tool and emits `BudgetDebited` events recording
    the agent-reported `total_tokens` post-dispatch
    (AC.A8.4). On dispatch close, transitions the scope to
    `completed | failed | cancelled` (AC.A8.5). On gate-chain
    refusal, returns a structured refusal value with code +
    rejecting gate + reason (AC.A8.7) without invoking the
    underlying `Agent`.
  - Retries open distinct scopes; cost ledger does not
    double-count (AC.A8.8).
  - Orchestrator unreachable → NDJSON diagnostic +
    unwrapped fallback dispatch (AC.A8.6).

AC surface (AC.A8.1 – AC.A8.S + AC.A8.A1 / AC.A8.A2 /
AC.A8.A3) —
outcome-shaped per locked plan §5. Test files mirror the
